A version under history/ numbered minor whose compatibility with the one
before it the checker cannot decide: cut numbers such a tip major, so it was
not cut so, and the immutability violation says it cannot be shown
compatible rather than that it is not.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	a: int
	b: int & >=a
}
-- ship/history/0.1.thema --
Schema: {
	a: int
	b: int & >a
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	a: int
	b: int & >a
}
-- out/error --
error[E0207]: immutability violation: history/0.1.thema cannot be shown backward compatible with history/0.0.thema
 --> history/0.1.thema:1:1
  |
1 | Schema: {
  | ^^^^^^
...
3 |     b: int & >a
  |     - b is constrained by a in both schemas, differently; the checker cannot compare constraints between fields
  |
 ::: history/0.0.thema:1:1
  |
1 | Schema: {
  | ------ the version before it
  |
  = note: 0.1 is a minor version, so it must accept all data 0.0 accepts
